        },
        {
          name: 'Pick Sara AI if...',
          body: 'you want the 11 pm enquiry on WhatsApp or Instagram to end as a booked appointment in your Google Calendar with the deposit already paid, without migrating your calendar or adding front-desk staff. Sara also reactivates patients, fills freed slots from a waitlist, asks for reviews and creates your Instagram content. It never touches patient records, on purpose.',
        },
      ],
    },
    proof: {
      title: 'The only case we publish is a real&nbsp;one',
      body: 'We do not invent logos or testimonials. ViaLaser (laser hair removal, Uruguay) has Sara answering its WhatsApp, Instagram and website live: 7 out of 10 appointments are booked by Sara.',
      cta: 'See the ViaLaser case',
    },
    ctaInline: { title: 'Compare with a demo of your own&nbsp;business.', cta: 'See my demo' },
    faq: [
      {
        q: 'What is the best AI assistant for an aesthetic clinic?',
        a: 'It depends on the problem you want to solve. If the bottleneck is the conversation (answering in time, booking and collecting the deposit on WhatsApp and Instagram), Sara is the most complete option. If you need patient records and invoicing, look at Doctocliq or AgendaPro. In Brazil with your own management software, Cloudia.',
      },
      {
        q: 'Do I have to change my scheduling software to use an AI assistant?',
        a: 'With most of them, yes: Soyla requires Doctocliq, Kura uses its own calendar and AgendaPro means migrating to their system. Sara works on top of the Google Calendar your clinic already uses, with no migration.',
      },
      {
